================================================================================
Origin and acknowledgement
================================================================================

andes started as an effort to optimize MS-GF+ and is now an independent search
algorithm of its own.

We gratefully acknowledge MS-GF+ and the open-source proteomics search engines
whose work has informed the field and ours:

  - MS-GF+    (Kim & Pevzner, Nat Commun 2014;5:5277)
  - a comparison engine     (Eng, Jahan & Hoopmann, Proteomics 2013)
  - a comparison search engine      (Lazear, J. Proteome Res. 2023)
  - the classic hyperscore engine  (Craig & Beavis, Bioinformatics 2004)

The bundled N-glycan structure databases under `crates/andes-glyco/glycan-db/`
are redistributed from pGlyco3 (https://github.com/pFindStudio/pGlyco3), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Their origin is acknowledged here to
satisfy Apache-2.0 §4's notice requirement:

  - pGlyco  (Liu et al., Nat. Commun. 2017;8:15473)
